{#- One check mark for the whole feature. The toggle on a session page, the
    chip on the grid and the mark on a card all draw this same path, so that
    marking a session, filtering for the marked ones and spotting one in the
    grid read as one thing rather than three that happen to agree.

    No width/height attributes: every context wants a different size and sets
    it in CSS. The stroke follows currentColor for the same reason - pressed,
    dimmed and resting states are all just a colour on the parent.

    Set `checkClass` before including to hang a context class on it. #}
<svg class="check{% if checkClass %} {{ checkClass }}{% endif %}" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3.25 8.4 6.6 11.75 12.75 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
